Linear FP16 Gaussian backdrop blur for the existing wlroots Vulkan renderer.
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
Local implementation for notdevblue, 2026-11-07.

Original normalized separable Gaussian compute shader: sigma 6.3, radius 24
output-buffer pixels. Fits original SceneFX blur_passes=2 / blur_radius=3
measured edge spread, with no decimation, transfer curves or HDR clamps.
Horizontal dispatch includes the vertical kernel halo; both passes stay within
that target domain. Two full-resolution FP16 scratch images belong to each
output target, and pipeline objects belong to the renderer. Unsupported compute
queues or FP16 storage formats return a no-op, never the rejected blit filter.

Scene-prefix suspend/resume design reference (no shader/pipeline code copied):
https://github.com/Seafoam-Labs/Aqueous/blob/e32ab7fc8f6510b393780b811ef92fe1bac6438e/docs/architecture-decisions/0001-vulkan-render-seam.md
Visible blur uses full-frame prefix reconstruction rather than damage caches.

